### \(\psi(2S)\) analysis

The data set used for the \(\psi(2S)\) analysis is the same as used in the J/\(\psi\) analysis. Also, the online trigger is BHT1 trigger as used in the J/\(\psi\) analysis. The di-electron decay branch ratio for \(\psi(2S)\) is (7.72 \(\pm\) 0.17)\(\times\)10\({}^{-3}\), which is about an order of magnitude lower than J/\(\psi\). But due to the high enhancement of the electron rich sample in the BHT1 trigger events, we can still reconstruct the \(\psi(2S)\) in the di-electron decay channel.

